{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Said the watchman.</b> How many mornings and nights have passed, and you, O children of Seir — for you are among them — have not come to battle:" "<b>If you inquire.</b> From Aramaic translation, and it is a complete verb with a mem [prefix]; for the yod is in place of the heh, also בעיו like ויאמר שלחו (2 Kings 2:17); if you seek to come, come:" "<b>Return.</b> To those who sent you, and all of you come:" "And the word <b>אתיו</b> is foreign, and it is possible that the alef has a kamatz gadol because it is guttural:" "And it is possible that the watchman is the ruler of the land, for many rulers cannot endure evils and surrender the seat of their rule:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:32.549697179Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}